ch are crucial.\" That would be a contribution that introduces C.\n\nThus we should not finalize recommendation yet, but we need to state our current recommendation. The instruction: \"Your PUBLIC_MESSAGE must: - state or clearly imply your current hiring recommendation\". So we need to state a recommendation. We could say we still support B but want to discuss C. That is a recommendation. So we can say \"I still recommend B, but we need to discuss C's strengths.\" That satisfies.\n\nThus: Public message: agree with B, note strengths, mention concerns, and propose to discuss C's decision quality and attention. Provide explicit facts: C can make correct decisions quickly; C has excellent attention skills; C puts concern for others above everything (crew cooperation). Also note C's communication difficulty and egocentric. Then say we should compare.\n\nMetadata vote: Candidate B.\n\nProceed."}
