perative behavior and weak memory for numbers (attention). Candidate C has excellent attention (explicit) and decision quality, and calm in crisis. That seems more aligned with safety-critical criteria. So perhaps we should shift recommendation to Candidate C.\n\nWe need to reference prior discussion: Agent 1 and 3 recommended B, but we can argue that C's strengths outweigh B's concerns. Provide explicit facts: C can make correct decisions quickly, keeps calm in crisis, excellent attention skills, puts concern for others above everything. Concern: difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric, not willing to further education. Compare to B's concerns: nasty remarks, weak memory for numbers. Which is more serious? Communication difficulty vs nasty remarks? Both affect crew cooperation. But C's \"puts concern for others above everything\" suggests good crew cooperation despite communication difficulty. B's nasty remarks directly harm crew cooperation. Also B's weak memory for numbers could affect attention accuracy. C has excellent attention. So C may be better.\n\nThus we can change vote to Candidate C.\n\nWe should also note that we still need to discuss A and D later.\n\nThus public message: I disagree with B as leading, propose C as stronger overall, citing facts, and note remaining candidates.\n\nProceed.\n\nNo tool needed.\n\nNow produce output."}
